# Team workflow (trust404 ⇄ T404)

Human contract: `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Repo brief: `AGENTS.md`. Subagent rules: `docs/agents/grok-subagent-guardrails.md`.

## Git

- `main` is protected. Never `git push origin main`. Work on a branch, open a PR, let `ci` go
  green, squash-merge. This applies to the orchestrating agent too.
- One topic per PR; the PR title is the changelog line.
- Do not commit another session's or another person's working-tree files. Add paths explicitly;
  never `git add -A` / `git add .`.
- Tags `submission-*` publish the judge image; only create one after `bench run detector --repeat 2`
  and the full pytest suite (with `DETECTOR_DOCKER_TESTS=1`) are green on the exact commit.

## Two engines

- `detector/` (Python, Slither IR) is ours; `noexit/` (TypeScript AST, from `ghwo336/T404`) is
  Hojae's. Do not edit `noexit/**` in this repo — changes go upstream to T404 and are re-vendored
  with the `UPSTREAM` commit bumped. Do not edit `detector/**` from the T404 side.
- `tools/ensemble.py`, `run.sh`, root `Dockerfile` are shared: propose, do not land alone.
- The judge-run invariants in `CONTRIBUTING.md` (stdout array, offline, any uid, read-only rootfs,
  46 solc pins, OZ v4+v5, budget) are acceptance criteria, not preferences. A PR that regresses one
  is a bug even if the score goes up.

## Numbers

- No score claim without a `bench run` on this corpus, naming tool, commit, tier set, and whether
  it is the organizers' +1/0/−1 or BAYBENCH weighted.
- A Tier 0 verdict moving away from the organizers' label is a stop, not a trade-off.
- Any Tier 1/3 verdict change needs a `labels.yaml` amendment with the organizers' rule cited and a
  `docs/bench/misses.md` row, in the same PR.
- Never run two `bench run` concurrently (shared `.bench_work/`).

## Reviewing a teammate's PR

- Reproduce the claimed number on the current `main` before commenting on it.
- Review as a comment with measurements; approve / request-changes is the human's call.
- Prefer "split this into N PRs" over "fix these 12 things" when the diff exceeds one topic.
